              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to MICHAEL B. KIMBERLY, petitioner Kentel Myrone Weaver argues that trial counsel failed to preserve a structural error, which is the gravest type of constitutional error in a criminal trial."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "MICHAEL B. KIMBERLY",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a885200f5f06081291f85300686ac4f5331afda76d69a91a1ddc25f85a4d337d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a885200f5f06-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to MICHAEL B. KIMBERLY, because of that alleged structural error, it would be impossible for the defendant to obtain relief under Strickland v. Washington for ineffective assistance of counsel."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "MICHAEL B. KIMBERLY",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a885200f5f06081291f85300686ac4f5331afda76d69a91a1ddc25f85a4d337d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a885200f5f06-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to MICHAEL B. KIMBERLY, defendants must prove actual prejudice resulting from their attorney's deficiency."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Kimberly",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a885200f5f06081291f85300686ac4f5331afda76d69a91a1ddc25f85a4d337d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a885200f5f06-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 53,
              "start": 53
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Kimberly, petitioner questions whether a public\u2011trial violation occurred, citing Presley v. Georgia."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. RavitZ",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a885200f5f06081291f85300686ac4f5331afda76d69a91a1ddc25f85a4d337d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a885200f5f06-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. RavitZ, petitioner notes that the Court has not said a reasonable\u2011probability standard cannot be shown."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. O'Connell",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a885200f5f06081291f85300686ac4f5331afda76d69a91a1ddc25f85a4d337d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a885200f5f06-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. O'Connell, amicus counsel O\u2019Connell argues that any structural error leads to fundamental unfairness and unreliability in the trial outcome."
      }
    ],
